      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 no3 is stored per unit volume while WOA23 nitrate is per unit mass, so the nitracline gradient and the shared-unit section require conversion to a common concentration unit.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`no3` is archived in mol m-3 while WOA23 is µmol kg-1: convert to one basis before any differencing or the shared-unit section, using in-situ density from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` (`ref_pressure=None`), not `transform_unit`'s constant default, and state `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "The depth of the maximum gradient is scale-invariant: a constant ρ cancels exactly, but in-situ density grows with depth and shifts the located depth a little, so locate the nitracline on the native field and state which basis was used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
