      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The basin means depend on the chosen basin partition, and the fragment requires saying which partition is used; here the question specifies the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded into parent oceans.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin means use the WOA23 basin mask (`select_basin`, `load_basin_mask`) with `include_marginal_seas=True` (marginal seas folded into their parent ocean) and the surface labels applied through the column (`depth_dependent=False`); state these choices, and that the Ofx `basin` field is not in the local archive.",
        "Report whether the Southern Ocean is a separate basin or split among the three oceans, since each choice changes basin means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
