      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The model no3 fields are on native grids, so nitracline depth should be computed natively and regridded only for maps and the WOA23-grid pattern/RMSE comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute global and basin mean nitracline depths on each source's own grid with its own cell areas; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the maps, the pattern correlation and the RMSE, and state the regrid method ('conservative' going to a coarser grid).",
        "The nitracline is located at a vertical extremum and is quantised by each product's vertical grid (where the profile is smooth the maximum can jump between levels), so read the maps together with the gradient itself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
