      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The question calls all model fields native, but GFDL-ESM4's CMIP6 ocean output is gr (conservatively regridded), which affects masks and exactness, while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are gn.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 `no3` is `gr`, already remapped (conserve_order1) to 180×360, so its \"native-grid\" numbers are 1°-archive numbers on a regridded land–sea mask; state this.",
        "CESM2 (100 km) and MPI-ESM1-2-LR (250 km) differ about 2.5× in resolution, so sharp-gradient features of the nitracline are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
