      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "A global mean nitracline depth must be area-weighted over ocean cells rather than a simple cell average, and the fragment establishes OMIP's weighting rules for means and integrals.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global and basin means of nitracline depth must be area-weighted (`compute_basic_stat`, `op='area_weighted_mean'`) with weights masked to the same valid cells; an unweighted mean over a curvilinear or lat-lon grid is wrong.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the pattern correlation."
      ]
    },
