      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells carry the missing value 1e20, so CF masking must be applied before computing gradients, basin means, correlations and RMSE or those cells will dominate.",
      "status": "dropped",
      "notes": [
        "xarray decodes the 1e20 fill to NaN by default; anything read with `mask_and_scale=False` carries 1e20 at land, and masks differ between variables, so build each field's valid mask from the field itself.",
        "A hand-rolled weighted reduction returns 0.0 for all-land columns; mask each cell's weights to its valid data so land stays missing and out of the basin denominators."
